    "https://www.careerbeacon.com/": {
      "title": "Be Seen. Get Hired.",
      "description": "Search for Jobs on CareerBeacon | Find a Job You Love Search Jobs Search Employers Salary Tools Salary Guide Income Tax Calculator Salary Converter Minimum Hourly Wage Cost of Living Calculator Explore Demographics by Place Resources For students and new grads Blog FR For Employers Log In Sign Up Search Jobs Search Employers Salary Tools Salary Guide Income Tax Calculator Salary Converter Minimum Hourly Wage Cost of Living Calculator Explore Demographics by Place Resources For students and new grads Blog Log In Sign Up For Employers Français Be Seen. Get Hired. Be Seen. Get Hired. Daily Job Opportunities Across Canada! Job Title, Keywords, or Employer RECENT SEARCHES Job Title, Keywords, or Employer Find Jobs Skip the Search. Find Your Perfect Job. Smart matching that actually works. Job recommendations that match your resume Easy to get started - just upload your resume Discover your best fit and get a head start with AI profile matching Sign Up Now Sign Up Now What's in a salary? Understand your salary better See your salary breakdown by hourly, monthly, and yearly earnings. Convert Salary But what's left for me? Calculate your take-home pay and see the tax deductions in your region. Calculate Taxes How far will my salary go? Explore the average cost of living in different cities and compare it with your salary. Use Calculator View minimum wage by province/territory in 2026 Check out the current and upcoming minimum hourly wage by province/territory. See Minimum Wages Frequently Asked Questions How do I search for jobs? Use the search bar at the top of the page to search for keywords, a job title, employer, and/or location and CareerBeacon will give you the most relevant search results. How does the \"Am I a Good Fit?\" feature work? The \"Am I a Good Fit?\" feature instantly analyzes your profile against job requirements to provide a detailed match assessment. This helps you focus on positions where you're most likely to succeed and highlights any potential skill gaps. What are the benefits of creating a MyBeacon account? You'll get personalized AI-powered job alerts based on your career preferences. The \"Am I A Good Fit?\" feature will help you quickly see how well your experience matches a job. You can also save jobs, upload your resume for faster applications, and stay updated on new opportunities that fit your skills. What is MyBeacon? MyBeacon is your personalized job search assistant that uses AI technology to match you with the most relevant jobs on CareerBeacon. It analyzes your skills, experience, and preferences to provide tailored job recommendations and insights about your fit for specific positions. Is MyBeacon free to use? Yes, MyBeacon is completely free for job seekers. Simply sign up with your existing CareerBeacon account or create a new account to access all personalized features. How accurate are MyBeacon's job matches? MyBeacon uses advanced AI technology to analyze multiple factors including your desired job title, salary expectations, and location preferences to provide highly relevant matches. The more information you provide, the more accurate your matches become. Who are the top employers hiring right now? CareerBeacon is always adding jobs from top employers across Canada like Bell , and NL Health Services . For a complete list of our Top Employers, head to our Top Employers page. What's my salary after taxes? Your after-tax salary depends on which province/territory you live in. To calculate your after-tax salary, use our Tax Calculator . What's my salary per hour? Use the CareerBeacon Salary Calculator to calculate your hourly, weekly, biweekly, monthly, and annual salary. What's the average cost of living in Canada? The average cost of living in Canada is $2,079/month (excluding rent). To see how far a salary can go in cities across Canada, visit our Cost of Living Calculator . How do you help employers? CareerBeacon has a variety of tools to help employers connect with jobseekers, promote their employer brand and job postings, and manage applicants as they apply for jobs. As an employer, how do I post a job? Use the CareerBeacon Post a Job tool to get a job posting in front of jobseekers in just a few clicks. Where can I find student jobs, summer positions, internships or co-ops? You can find student jobs, summer positions, internships, and co-op opportunities on our new CareerBeacon Launchpad portal . It's designed to connect you with a variety of employment options tailored for students and recent grads. For Jobseekers Get Hired Search Jobs Students & Recent Grads Browse Jobs Search Employers Explore Demographics by Place Income Tax Calculator Salary Converter Cost of Living Calculator Income Tax Calculator Minimum Hourly Wage 2026 Career Advice For Employers Post a Job Applicant Tracking System Recruitment Marketing Services Job Description Generator Job Post Visualizer Contact Sales About Us Who We Are Blog Contact Us Terms of Service Privacy Policy Latest Updates Announcement English | Français © 2026  CareerBeacon.  All rights reserved. English Français For Jobseekers Get Hired Search Jobs Students & Recent Grads Browse Jobs Search Employers Explore Demographics by Place Income Tax Calculator Salary Converter Cost of Living Calculator Salary Guide Minimum Hourly Wage 2026 Career Advice For Employers Post a Job Applicant Tracking System Recruitment Marketing Services Job Description Generator Job Post Visualizer Contact Sales About Us Who We Are Blog Contact Us Terms of Service Privacy Policy Latest Updates © 2026  CareerBeacon.  All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://nscad.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Vacancy-Notice-for-Fall-2026_-Individual-Course-Appointment_v6.pdf": {
      "title": "teaching philosophy and an artist statement, and a portfolio with 20 examples of your",
      "description": "NSCAD University \nFounded in Halifax in 1887, NSCAD University is an international centre of excellence for \nthe study, practice, and teaching of the visual arts. All qualified applicants are encouraged \nto apply; however, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given priority. \nHiring will be in accordance with NSCAD University’s policy on non- discrimination. For \nmore information, please visit https://nscad.ca/ \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nApplication Deadline \n \n \n \n \nDirect Applications To \nVACANCY NOTICE FOR  FALL 2026 (INDIVIDUAL COURSE APPOINTMENTS) \nAdvancing the visual arts \n \nThe following courses for Fall  2026 are currently unassigned to Full-  time, Pro- Rated, \nor Sessional faculty members. Individuals who feel they are qualified to teach any of \nthe listed courses are asked to submit an application to amasterson@nscad.ca  Office \nof Academic Affairs  and Research specifying the course(s) for which they wish to be \nconsidered. Applicants should include a current curriculum vitae, a statement of \nteaching philosophy and an artist statement, and a portfolio with 20 examples of your \nwork in digital format (JPEG or PDF preferred). AHIS applicants should include a CV and \nstatement of teaching philosophy. \n \n \nAugust 20, 2026 (Review of applications will begin immediately) \nFor additional information on the above courses, please consult Self-Serve Courses for \ncourse times and descriptions. Salary will be in accordance with the Part-Time Faculty \nSalary Grid. \n \nAnne Masterson \nAcademic Affairs Officer \nOffice of Academic Affairs and Research \nEmail:    amasterson@nscad.ca\nNSCAD University \n5163 Duke Street, Halifax, NS, B3J 3J6 \n \n \n \n    2026F EDAR-5610-1SP Secondary Art Methods 1  Thurs 1:30PM-4:30PM \n     \n \n \n"
    },
