e admission requirements Certificate Admission Requirements Application checklist Transfer, articulation and pathway agreements Building your portfolio Financing your education Financing Your Education Tuition and fees Scholarships and bursaries Living in Halifax International applications Meet with us Open House Book a tour Recruitment events Talk with a recruiter Programs Why study at NSCAD Facility Overview Facility Overview Physical accessibility at NSCAD Study or work abroad Undergraduate programs Undergraduate programs Foundation Art History (Studio) Interdisciplinary Design Ceramics Art History (Non-Studio) Expanded Media Film FINE ART – DRAWING FINE ART – PAINTING FINE ART – PRINTMAKING Fine Art – Sculpture Interdisciplinary  Arts Jewellery+Metalsmithing Photography Textiles+Fashion Graduate programs Graduate programs Master of Arts in Art Education Master of Design Master of Fine Arts Certificate programs Certificate programs Post Baccalaureate Certificate in Design Visual arts certificate for teachers Visual Arts Certificate in Studio Pre-university studies Student Experience New Students Orientation Welcome Weeks Academic Resources NSCAD Academic Calendar Academic Advising Important Dates Forms Graduation Information Learning Commons Outgoing Student Exchange Registration information Writing centre Web Access Finances Financing Your Education Tuition Scholarships and Bursaries Student Support Accessibility Health Coverage & Care Housing Information Mental Health and Wellness Opportunity and Belonging Raise a Concern or Complaint Campus Life and Events Our Campuses Events Anna Leonowens Gallery Visiting Artists Student Art Award NSCAD Design Shift Award MAYHEM Festival Student Union NSCAD Art Supply Store Shops, Studios, Equipment Library About About Us + Vision and Mission Senior Management Academic Plan Facilities Management Price Awards for Excellence in Teaching Governance Board of Governors Presidential Search Committee Senate Faculty and Academic Support Directory Equity, Diversity, Inclusion & Accessibility Statement against hate and discrimination Labour Relations Research at NSCAD Strategic Research Plan Canada Research Chairs Research Creation Research Support and Granting Councils Visit and Explore Our Campuses Our City Virtual Tour Campus Maps Alumni Alumni VIVID Newsletter NSCAD Alumni at Work Alumni Profiles Alumni Ring Design Challenge 2026 Alumni Association Alumni Association Honorary degrees Give Connect Navigator Careers EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITIES NSCAD University employs 85 regular full-time and part-time faculty, 30 educational resource personnel, 60 staff members and more than 50 individual course instructors in a creative working environment. We offer opportunities to influence the next generation of art and design, create a healthy working atmosphere and to inspire the rule breakers, the dreamers, the makers, the innovators, the exceptional and the forever curious. Working at NSCAD is a vibrant, stimulating and exciting place to be. To inspire the extraordinary, we have to be the extraordinary. Can you add to that? If you can, then we have the perfect atmosphere for you to grow. Please review our open positions and vacancy notices for opportunities to join the NSCAD community Job opportunities Job Title Location Category Apply No jobs available Additional Positions Individual Course Appointments (Fall 2026) HIRING PRACTICES Recruitment and hiring practices at NSCAD University do not discriminate against any candidate with respect to hiring on the basis of race, colour, sex, marital status, sexual orientation, citizenship (except where required by the Immigration Act), physical handicap (as defined in the Nova Scotia Human Rights Act), age, creed, ethnic or national origin, religion, political affiliation and political beliefs (provided such do not interfere with the operation of the university), or membership or non-membership in one of the university’s unions. Excellence, diversity and equity form the foundation of the University’s hiring objectives and practices, and the vacancy goals for achieving diversity and employment equity among its faculty and staff are realized through equity outreach and due consideration of qualified candidates. NSCAD is committed to achieving and maintaining a workforce that reflects and affirms the diversity of our society and works together in providing a discrimination-free environment, characterized by respect and equity, where people can exercise their individual potential. CONNECT Talk with a recruiter VIRTUAL VISIT Academic calendar Apply to NSCAD 5163 Duke Street Halifax, NS B3J 3J6 Canada +1 902.444.9600 +1 902.425.2420 info@nscad.ca Land Acknowledgement NSCAD University is located in Kjipuktuk, the district of Sipekne’katik, Mi’kma’ki, which since time immemorial, has been the unceded traditional territory and ancestral homelands of the Mi’kmaq Nation. In Nova Scotia, we recognize we are all Treaty People. Read our Land Acknowledgement. NSCAD acknowledges the historical and contemporary presence of people of African descent. African Nova Scotians have existed and persisted on the traditional land of the Mi’kmaq for more than 400 years. Read our People’s Acknowledgement. Contact us Important dates Explore careers Access & Privacy Security Follow us Instagram Facebook Linkedin"
    },
    "https://nscad.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Vacancy-Notice-for-Winter-2027_-Individual-Course-Appointment_v2.pdf": {
      "title": "teaching philosophy and an artist statement, and a portfolio with 20 examples of your",
      "description": " \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nApplication Deadline \n \n \n \n \nDirect Applications To \nVACANCY NOTICE FOR WINETR 2027 (INDIVIDUAL COURSE APPOINTMENTS) \nAdvancing the visual arts \n \nThe following courses for Winter 2027 are currently unassigned to Full- time, Pro- Rated, \nor Sessional faculty members. Individuals who feel they are qualified to teach any of the \nlisted courses are asked to submit an application to amasterson@nscad.ca  Office of \nAcademic Affairs  and Research specifying the  course(s) for which they wish to be \nconsidered. Applicants should include a current curriculum vitae, a statement of \nteaching philosophy and an artist statement, and a portfolio with 20 examples of your \nwork in digital format (JPEG or PDF preferred). AHIS applicants should include a CV and \nstatement of teaching philosophy. \n \n \nSeptember 24, 2026 (Review of applications will begin immediately) \nFor additional information on the above courses, please consult Self-Serve Courses for \ncourse times and descriptions. Salary will be in accordance with the Part-Time Faculty \nSalary Grid. \n \nAnne Masterson \nAcademic Affairs Officer \nOffice of Academic Affairs and Research \nEmail:    amasterson@nscad.ca\nNSCAD University \n5163 Duke Street, Halifax, NS, B3J 3J6 \n \n \n \nCourse Code Course Title Day(s) Start End \nARTS-3110-OL1X/CRFT-3110-OL1X Entrepreneurship for Vis. Arts Tues 1:00PM 4:00PM \nCERM-2001-1 Introductory Ceramics Thurs 8:30AM 12:30PM \nCERM-3101-1 Intermediate Handbuilding Tues 1:00PM 5:00PM \nCRFT-1010-1X/DSGN-1010-1X  Material Exploration & Express (Ceramics) Wed 1:00PM 5:00PM \nCRFT-1010-2X/DSGN-1010-2X Material Exploration & Express (Jewellery) Wed 1:00PM 5:00PM \nDSGN-1040-1 Digital Tools for Interaction Wed 6:00PM 9:00PM \nDSGN-1510-1 Creativity in Design Practice Mon 8:30AM 12:30PM \nDSGN-3318-1 Advanced Typography & Branding Wed 1:00PM 5:00PM \nEDAR-5050-1SP Visual Arts in Classroom Mon 9:00AM 12:00PM \nEDAR-5050-2SP Visual Arts in Classroom Mon 1:30PM 4:30PM \nEDAR-5050-3SP Visual Arts in Classroom Mon 9:00AM 12:00PM \nEDAR-5050-4SP Visual Arts in Classroom Mon 1:30PM 4:30PM \nEDAR-5650-1 Guided Methods II Wed 6:00PM 9:00PM \nFILM-3300-1 Screenwriting Studio Wed 1:00PM 5:00PM \nFILM-3340-1 Production Design Film Mon 1:00PM 5:00PM \nFILM-3461-1 Stop Motion Animation Wed 1:00PM 5:00PM \nFILM-3500-1 Film 2 Tues/Fri 1:00PM 5:00PM \nJWLY-2000-1 Introduction to Jewellery Tues 1:00PM 5:00PM \nJWLY-2000-2 Introduction to Jewellery Thurs 5:30PM 9:30PM \nJWLY-2100-1 Introduction to Holloware Fri 8:30AM 12:30PM \nJWLY-2500-1 Jewellery II: Methods Thurs 8:30AM 12:30PM \nJWLY-2700-1 Enamelling Fri 8:30AM 12:30PM \nMDIA-2100-1 Introductory Printed Matter Tues 8:30AM 12:30PM \nPHOT-1000-2 Photo Thurs 8:30AM 12:30PM \nPHOT-1000-3 Photo Tues 5:30PM 9:30PM \nPHOT-3613-1 Sem: Photography Now Tues 8:30AM 12:30PM \nPRTM-1503-1 Foundations of Print Media Tues 1:00PM 5:00PM \nPRTM-3036-1 Artist Books II Mon/Tues 8:30AM 12:30PM \nTEXL-2010-1 Off-Loom Structures Fri 8:30AM 12:30PM \nTEXL-2501-1 Fashion Studio 1: Skills Dev. Tue 1:00PM 5:00PM \nTEXL-2502-1 Fashion Studio 2: Techn. Dev. Mon 8:30AM 12:30PM \n \n \n \n\n \nNSCAD University \nFounded in Halifax in 1887, NSCAD University is an international centre of excellence for \nthe study, practice, and teaching of the visual arts. All qualified applicants are encouraged \nto apply; however, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given priority. \nHiring will be in accordance with NSCAD University’s policy on non- discrimination. For \nmore information, please visit https://nscad.ca/ "
    },
