    "https://jobs.careerbeacon.com/details/human-resources-director/2240917?utm_source=NSCAD+University&utm_medium=widget&utm_campaign=refer&utm_content=2240917&utm_term=jobtitle": {
      "title": "Human Resources Director",
      "description": "Human Resources Director at NSCAD University | Careerbeacon.com NSCAD University Human Resources Director Halifax, NS Apply Later Apply Now Discover The Opportunity Halifax, NS In-person Human Resources and Recruiting Management Full-time $101,301 - $132,175 / year Benefits: Health Insurance Dental Insurance Paid Time Off Flexible Work Pension plan Group RRSP Retirement Plans Life Insurance Disability Insurance Employee Assistance Program Tuition Aid Commuter Perks The Director of Human Resources is a strategic member of the leadership team and responsible for providing expert advice, oversight, leadership and support for the human resources activities of the university including recruitment and retention, labour relations, training and development, policy development, conflict resolution, human resources reporting, management support, and compensation administration and oversight. The position is a strategic partner with the AVP, VP and President portfolios and provides guidance and support on HR policy development and implementation. Share What you'll do Responsibilities Provides strategic leadership and oversight of the University's human resources functions, policies, programs, and services. Leads recruitment, hiring, onboarding, employee relations, performance management, and other employment processes across the University. Provides strategic advice and guidance to senior leaders and managers on employee relations, compensation, performance, discipline, and workplace matters. Leads labour relations and collective bargaining, including interpretation and implementation of collective agreements, negotiations, grievances, classification, and liaison with union representatives. Oversees payroll, benefits, pensions, employee leave administration, and related HR information systems and processes, ensuring accuracy, compliance, and effective service delivery. Leads the development, implementation, and review of HR policies, procedures, programs, and initiatives in alignment with institutional priorities and applicable legislation. Oversees employee training, orientation, professional development, occupational health and safety, and other workplace programs. Ensures compliance with employment legislation, regulatory requirements, immigration processes, reporting obligations, and applicable institutional and collective agreement requirements. Represents Human Resources on senior leadership, governance, and institutional committees and works collaboratively with internal and external stakeholders. Develops and manages the HR budget, prepares reports and analysis for senior management and the Board, and provides strategic recommendations on human resources matters. What you'll need Qualifications An undergraduate degree with specialization in human resources is required. A Master's degree and CHRP designation are preferred. A minimum of five years' experience at a management level in a relevant work setting is required including: Sound judgement and discretion, and a proven ability to assess and resolve complex and/or sensitive issues. Experience working in a unionized environment, interpreting collective agreements, and negotiating as part of a bargaining team and/or lead negotiator. Conflict resolution and mediation skills are beneficial. Experience with policy development. Knowledge of benefit plans, disability processing, plan design and benefit rate costing is advantageous. Knowledge of Nova Scotia labour law, privacy legislation, human rights, pension and health and safety legislation. Strong strategic planning, problem-solving, negotiation, facilitation, and organization skills. Ability to work independently and to plan, implement and manage multiple projects simultaneously and accurately. Experience working and maintaining a complex HRIS system and various employee groups. Exceptional interpersonal, written and speaking skills. Proficiency with spreadsheets, Internet, database and word processing software. A little bit about us NSCAD University NSCAD University and Halifax are in Mi'kma'ki, on the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi'kmaq Nation. NSCAD University is committed to reconciliation and to building respectful relationships with Indigenous peoples and with the African Nova Scotian communities that have been enriching this region for 400 years. As a small school with three urban campuses, and programs across a range of fine arts, craft, design, and media arts, NSCAD University is an incubator for talent and an active contributor to the arts scene in Canada's fastest-growing city. Since 1887, NSCAD has been a leader in visual arts education in Canada, with distinguished alumni building careers all over the world. Are you interested? Work With Us Applications should be sent via the CareerBeacon website. Applications should include a cover letter and detailed CV. Deadline for applications: The University will begin considering applicants on October 19, 2026. We appreciate all applicants, however, only those selected to move forward in the competittion will be contacted. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadian citizens and permanent residents of Canada will be given priority in this search. NSCAD university encourages applications from Indigenous persons, racially visible persons, persons with a disability, women, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. Apply Now View Careers Page Powered by Apply Later Enter your email to receive a reminder to apply for this position at a later date. * Email Apply Later We will send you an email reminder to with a link to this job. Cancel Create Reminder"
    },
